/-- DERIVED. `Write for Vec<u8>`: append the bytes and report that all of them were written.
    Rust's `Vec<u8>` writer cannot fail -- it grows to fit -- so the only non-`Ok` path here is
    the length guard, which exists because Aeneas's `Vec` carries a `length ≤ usize::MAX`
    invariant. Exceeding it is unreachable in this program (the ext-data preimage is a few
    hundred bytes), and `fail` is the honest encoding of "cannot happen".
    Source: '/rustc/library/std/src/io/impls.rs', lines 483:4-483:56 -/
@[rust_fun "std::io::impls::{std::io::Write<alloc::vec::Vec<u8>>}::write"]
def alloc.vec.VecU8.Insts.StdIoWrite.write
